- WHY “Invalid field format” ERROR OCCURS
  *–––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––*
- The error happens because:
- 
- 1. Screen field is defined as NUMC (numeric only)
- 1. User enters “PR02” (contains letters)
- 1. SAP dynpro validation rejects it BEFORE PAI module runs
- 
- SOLUTIONS:
- 
- Option A: Change screen field format to CHAR
- - In SE51, change field format from NUMC to CHAR
- - Keep data element as IM_POSNR
- - Validation in PAI converts POSID → POSNR
- 
- Option B: Use dropdown list (VRM_SET_VALUES)
- - Populate dropdown with POSNR values
- - Display text shows “PR02 - Program Name”
- - When selected, field gets POSNR (00000011)
- - User never types anything
- 
- Option C: Use search help (F4IF_INT_TABLE_VALUE_REQUEST)
- - User clicks F4 help
- - Sees list with POSID
- - System fills in POSNR
- 
- RECOMMENDED: Option B (Dropdown) - matches FDS “Selected by user”
